A||||3||rockcrawl||Seeing double?.....2 Blue GTs in one day!||||14||
Z||000000||rockcrawl||08-12-2000||08:34 AM||||I'm on the road a lot for work, unfortunately not driving my Fieros. Anyway, while driving through Slatington PA, I see a blue GT fastback coming up behind me. I turned left and he passed me on the right. I decided right there that if I ever had another Fiero that needed a paint job, it would be blue. The blue over silver looked great. I can't remember the last time I saw any blue Fiero. Much to my surprise, about 30 min later I saw another Blue GT in Jim Thorpe PA!! I was amazed! It was definately a different car because this one had a bra on the nose, and some pink lettering on the back. How many of you guys have a blue Fiero? Anyone know production numbers? I just looked and I see blue was not an option for '86, so they must have been '87s?<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'86 GT 3800 (for sale)<BR>'87 GT (noisey 2.8)<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<p>[This message has been edited by rockcrawl (edited 08-12-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000001||My7Fieros||08-12-2000||12:57 PM||||That color was called either bright blue metallic or medium blue metallic, I cant quite remember which. I bought some about 6 months ago to paint my 87 GT with (its now an old faded gold, and I already have a gold GT) but like I said Id have to go look at the can and its at a friend's garage.<BR>Anyway, it was only made in 87, only for the Fiero, and only for the GT model. There was another blue in 87 for the notchback models, but it wasnt metalic (or not very metallic).<BR>Dumbest thing Pontiac did was to discontinue that color......no, wait, that was the SECOND dumbest thing they ever did!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||6
